{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_04115f1de140056c833e22ab498342411f9de61ca60aa63e2968b59a4ade8bd1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Mac/Linux the CLI installs via a curl-piped shell script, and on Windows via a PowerShell one-liner fetching install.ps1."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1a4f339e0210a86bc4e23b93d223caaca7ad2520bcded444a04237244e5f46a5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Codex CLI can also be installed through npm (@openai/codex) and Homebrew (brew install --cask codex), or by downloading platform binaries from GitHub Releases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7a850c1df144fadce442e2744c5c922febb1dc34891c4f7f157a06cf82e766c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Standalone installers default to downloads from releases.openai.com/codex and fall back to GitHub Releases; setting CODEX_INSTALLER_USE_RELEASES_OPENAI_COM=false forces GitHub Releases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8dd0b86d8f1e4d8a4df8ee6f1e48a4dbc79b588753a1de38e54b0f0aa69ff945"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Authentication supports signing in with a ChatGPT account (recommended for Plus/Pro/Business/Edu/Enterprise plans) or, with extra setup, an API key."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b81ae7fa3f3152a9d6025f167edc84cdfad7f682e8498cea7be248faf9102608"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is Apache-2.0 licensed and links to external docs for configuration, sandboxing/approvals, execution policy, skills, and AGENTS.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c0d9169e44929b3b0cf7c5e748c6caef777c8e51f27820ae3172a39da74730a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Codex CLI is a local coding agent from OpenAI, started by running the `codex` command; a desktop app experience is available via `codex app`."}],"claim_ids":["clm_04115f1de140056c833e22ab498342411f9de61ca60aa63e2968b59a4ade8bd1","clm_1a4f339e0210a86bc4e23b93d223caaca7ad2520bcded444a04237244e5f46a5","clm_7a850c1df144fadce442e2744c5c922febb1dc34891c4f7f157a06cf82e766c2","clm_8dd0b86d8f1e4d8a4df8ee6f1e48a4dbc79b588753a1de38e54b0f0aa69ff945","clm_b81ae7fa3f3152a9d6025f